id: pm-qckpnq
title: "GH-974: merge receipt preferred contradicts retained side under stable_value_order"
description: "Track GitHub issue #974: merge receipts emit top-level preferred=ours even when deterministic stable_value_order retains theirs, so structured agent consumers receive a self-contradictory outcome despite retained/discarded values being truthful."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-context,github,merge-safety
created_at: "2026-08-11T08:33:30.091Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-11T16:29:51.345Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:46.413Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-11T16:21:46.413Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: SDK and CLI receipts expose truthful requested preference and per-decision retained side; both merge directions converge and report the same value without contradictory fields; compatibility and merge-safety tests cover scalar equality and unequal values
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.10
repro_steps: "Create two branches that assign different priority values, merge in both directions, and compare preferred against decisions[].ours/theirs/retained/discarded."
resolution: Replaced ambiguous preferred receipt fields with requested_preference while preserving authoritative retained and discarded decisions and backward-compatible ingestion.
expected_result: Receipts distinguish requested preference from the actual retained side and remain internally consistent for direction-independent resolution.
actual_result: "Both merge directions converge under stable_value_order without claiming that the requested side survived; current receipts emit requested_preference only, while legacy preferred and pre-preference schema-v1 receipts remain readable."
component: SDK merge receipts
customer_impact: Agents can wrongly conclude their branch value survived and act on false merge context.
